course: dictionary
lesson: 3876
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on the sentence. Freak can be a noun, an adjective or a verb, and the context tells you which meaning is right. Look at the words around it and ask: what would fit here?
explain: «The freak storm knocked down trees across the town.» Here freak means very unusual and unexpected. The clue is storm: a storm is weather, not a person, so freak is describing the storm.
explain: «Mum is a neat freak, so she tidies her room every night.» A neat freak is someone who is very keen on being tidy. The clue is tidies: she is keen on tidiness, so freak means a person who loves something.
explain: Freak can also hurt people. Calling someone a freak means calling them strange or not normal, and that is name-calling. Words like this can make people feel sad, so if you hear it, tell a teacher or a trusted adult.
fact: Freak can be a noun, an adjective or a verb, so check the sentence before you decide what it means.
fact: «A freak accident» means an accident that is very unusual and unexpected.
fact: «A fitness freak» means a person who is very keen on exercise.
fact: «Freak out» means to become very scared, upset or excited.
fact: Calling a person a freak is rude and hurtful, and it is name-calling that we must never use.
exercise: «The freak storm knocked down trees across the town.» What does freak mean here? | Happy and excited | A person who is very keen on storms | *Very unusual and unexpected | Very scared
exercise: Ella says, «Dad is a control freak about the remote.» What does control freak mean? | A person who drops things often | A person who controls the weather | *A person who must be in charge of everything | A person who is scared of the dark
exercise: What is calling a classmate a freak? | *Hurtful name-calling | A sports game | A type of weather | A kind compliment
test: What does freak mean in «a freak accident»? | Slow and careful | Very keen on accidents | Angry and loud | *Unusual and unexpected
test: Maya says, «I freak out when I see spiders!» What does freak out mean? | Clean up the room | Fall asleep quickly | Go for a long walk | *Become very scared, upset or excited
exam: Someone calls your friend a freak. What is the best response? | Say nothing and forget it | Join in and laugh | Call them a freak back | *Be kind to your friend and tell a teacher or trusted adult
